# KiCad text formats — diffable as text (also what Prism's semantic diffing
# reads). Deliberately NO merge=union: union "resolves" a conflict by keeping
# both sides' lines with no conflict markers and reports a clean merge, so a
# corrupted schematic got committed with nothing flagging it. Default merging
# leaves <<<<<<< markers, which configure.py --check and CI both catch. The
# real protection is the one-owner-at-a-time convention in README.md.
*.kicad_sch text
*.kicad_pcb text
*.kicad_pro text
*.kicad_wks text
*.kicad_dru text

# Treat as generated/vendored: not shown in language stats, collapsed in
# diffs on GitHub's UI.
Logos/* -diff
*.step -diff -text
*.png -diff -text

# Force LF regardless of a Windows checkout's core.autocrlf setting. A CRLF
# shebang line (#!/bin/bash\r) fails to find the interpreter inside a Linux
# Docker container or CI runner — this bit us running kibot_launch.sh locally
# after checking it out on Windows.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.csv filter=bom_csv
*.html filter=bom_html
*.gbr filter=gerber
*.gbrjob filter=gbrjob
*.xml filter=xml
*.kicad_pcb filter=kicad_pcb_f
*.net filter=net_filter
